A||||14||DJRice||Dew Wipe Removal/Replacement||||10||
Z||000000||DJRice||02-28-2000||09:34 AM||||This is a short and sweet but valuable tip.  If you want to replace your dew wipes, send Rodney Dickman the $9 ($7.50 + $1.50 Shipping) for his dew wipe removal tool.  I had both doors done in about 2 hrs. and thats including the time it took me to fish out the screws I dropped inside the door.  <P>The job was super quick and easy thanks to that little tool.  <P>BTW, Criswell Chevrolet has the wipes in stock, the set cost $45 after shipping and took less than a week to get.||||reg||10
Z||000001||AL||02-28-2000||08:43 PM||||thats good, but what i did i bent a small screw driver and i took the screws off in no time||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||02-28-2000||09:22 PM||||I took a small wrench, grinded down a phillps bit, then JB welded it in the wrench! Worked like a charm and did both sides and replaced screws with hexagon head screws for easier removal next time. If anyone wants the tool I made to get to the screws let me know. You can have it!||||reg||3
